{"id": "EUVD-2026-80816", "enisaUuid": "6566412c-0507-319b-ba92-7944776d3c34", "description": "reNgine through 2.2.0 contains an authorization bypass vulnerability in the GetFileContents API endpoint that allows any authenticated user to read bundled recon tool configuration files. Attackers with low-privilege Auditor roles can access files containing third-party API keys for services like SecurityTrails, Shodan, Censys, VirusTotal, BinaryEdge and Hunter by querying the endpoint without role-based permission checks.", "datePublished": "2026-09-16T14:40:49", "dateUpdated": "2026-09-24T14:22:43", "baseScore": 7.1, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:L/UI:N/VC:H/VI:N/VA:N/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://github.com/yogeshojha/rengine/issues/1554", "https://github.com/yogeshojha/rengine", "https://github.com/yogeshojha/rengine/blob/302b5f32e7aa5958fec9e405772f4aa069eb21a2/web/api/views.py#L1607-L1700", "https://github.com/yogeshojha/rengine/blob/302b5f32e7aa5958fec9e405772f4aa069eb21a2/web/reNgine/settings.py#L129-L141", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/rengine-through-2.2.0-unauthorized-configuration-file-read"], "aliases": ["GHSA-29ch-4262-w3fr", "CVE-2026-92570"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.44, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "cf16d9ce-7443-3f7a-a1ad-5c660e31d61b", "product": {"name": "rengine", "vendor": {"name": "rengine"}}, "product_version": "0 \u22642.2.0"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "244c6039-19b7-39be-85c4-2ebd5052e28c", "vendor": {"name": "yogeshojha"}}], "isExploited": false}